+	 *
+	 * Deferred packets are the exception and must survive. A slot in
+	 * tx_deferred_skb was only DMA-mapped by bam_dmux_netdev_start_xmit(),
+	 * never submitted, so the quiesce never had a descriptor of its own to
+	 * terminate and the mapping is still valid for the rebuilt channel.
+	 * Freeing them here -- which is what this function used to do -- threw
+	 * away the packet that start_xmit() had just deferred while waiting for
+	 * this very wake. bam_dmux_runtime_suspend() refuses to suspend while
+	 * tx_deferred_skb is non-zero (its Guard 1), so a deferred packet is
+	 * always meant to be drained by the wake, not discarded by it.
+	 *
+	 * Measured before this fix (patch 811 telemetry, one boot): 27 packets
+	 * deferred, 27 wiped with a live skb, 0 submitted. A single ping sent
+	 * to a collapsed modem was lost 3/3; the same ping sent while the modem
+	 * was awake was delivered.
 	 */
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dmux->tx_retry_work);
